# Shell scripts must have LF endings wherever they are checked out.
#
# A .sh file with CRLF fails on Linux with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env
# bash^M", which is a confusing way for a GitHub Action to break on the one
# platform most people run it on. Relying on each contributor's core.autocrlf
# is how that happens.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
